{"discussion":"I now have all source files. The bug is clear: windows.py DayWindow.contains() requires the entire shift to fit inside [midnight, next midnight). An overnight shift (e.g. 22:00–06:00) spans two calendar days, so it is never 'contained' in either day's window and is dropped from both reports. The fix: replace contains() with an overlap_minutes() that computes the intersection of the shift interval and the window interval, then add only those overlapping minutes in report_minutes().","operation":{"action":"patch","path":"src/shiftledger/windows.py","old":"    def contains(self, shift: Shift) -> bool:
        """Whether the entire shift interval is inside this window."""
        return self.start <= shift.start and shift.end <= self.end","new":"    def overlap_minutes(self, shift: Shift) -> float:
        """Minutes of the shift that fall within this window."""
        start = max(shift.start, self.start)
        end = min(shift.end, self.end)
        if start >= end:
            return 0.0
        return (end - start).total_seconds() / 60.0","expected_candidate_id":"b77c87956a3936ab169f80f5df55b4a2731b6015968fdebcb1e2a1095469c6ea","expected_file_sha256":"31768516afc033f5fe8c96a195f1b16cdf323359e9d1369c0a8db90e78c2880f"}}
